.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-COMMIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-commit
.Nd commit to a file now, to reveal it later
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis commit
.Op Fl -kind Cm randomisation | preregistration | other
.Op Fl -label Ar text
.Op Fl -after Ar time
.Op Fl o | Fl -out Ar salt
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar dir file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis commit
records in the data record of
.Ar dir
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
a commitment to
.Ar file ,
such as a randomisation list made before a trial or an analysis plan
written before the data are seen: the 64 hex digits of
.Bd -literal -offset indent
SHA3-256("noqtis-commit-1" || 0x00 || 32 as 8 bytes big-endian ||
         salt || the bytes of file)
.Ed
.Pp
with a fresh 32-byte salt from the operating system's random source,
written to
.Ar file Ns Pa .salt
(owner-only; or
.Fl o ;
.Fl f
replaces one).
Without the salt the digest says nothing of the file; with it anyone
can check that a file is the one committed to
.Pq Xr noqtis-reveal 1 .
Keep the file and its salt out of the capsule until the reveal, and
seal the capsule with a timestamp
.Pq Xr noqtis-seal 1 Fl -tsa
so the commitment has a date no one can move.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -kind
what the file is (default
.Cm other )
.It Fl -label
a short name for it
.It Fl -after
a UTC time
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
before which it is not to be revealed
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the commitment and the salt are written, 2 on a usage or file
error (an existing salt file without
.Fl f
among them).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-reveal 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqdcommit 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
